 saw him  hanji and captain levi then make a brief  appearance and the former has a shocked  expression on their face here because  levi pretty much looks like a corpse  towards the end of the last season the  captain was blown up after zeke  detonated the thunderspear that was  inside him but although he looks  terrible the trailer doesn't actually  confirm anything about whether he's dead  or alive  things then switch back over to  shiganshina as malian troops begin  parachuting into the district but this  is contrasted by the airships all being  on fire and elena here having the time  of her life i won't go into spoilers  about why the airships are like this but  it goes without saying that obviously  this is not something the marlins would  want to happen  this scene is followed by a quick moment  of gabby using the kart titan's mouth is  like her own personal taxi and i gotta  say the service looks a lot more  comfortable than the one zeke had to  deal with in season three  mikasa then appears with her thinking  face on as she's holding the scarf that  erin gave her when they were younger and  as you can tell from the background  she's still locked up at this time  after this the rest of the trailer is  mostly just very fast reaction shots  with my favorite being zeke desperately  calling out to someone as he stretches  out his hand because on his body his  time shifter marks are clearly visible  that confirms that at some point between  this screenshot and his last appearance  in the series which is when he was being  shoved into a titan stomach zeke  transformed into the beast titan at  least one more time  as i said the remainder of the trailer  is just people reacting to things some  more dramatically than others and the  final moment is aaron inside the attack  titan still fighting against reiner we  actually saw a very similar moment from  the first trailer for the final season  that came out ages ago so yeah this is  just a variation of that  anyway like i said in the intro there  was also a message from isayama  regarding part 2 which should be on  screen and the translation says i'm  really looking forward to the start of  the second half of the final season even  in the original the manga it was very  difficult drawing and i am very sorry  that mapper will have a hard time again  for many teams that the assistants had a  hard time with the difficult scenes are  the ones i'm looking forward to the most  and i hope that people who see it for  the first time in the anime will also  enjoy it  so from the way that sounds it's  basically like isaiah's apology that is  to map up for you know the spectacles  they've had to animate for the second  half of the season but hopefully even  though the scenes are super difficult  hopefully he can still do some justice  to the manga regardless thank you for  watching this breakdown of the very  short trailer for part two of the final  season and i hope it gave you a little  bit of insight or made you realize  something that you didn't see when  watching it for the first time like i  said be sure to sub if you want to see  weekly episode breakdowns when the  season starts back again and until the  next one peace out
 

